  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: One of the few 'soups' that you can eat without
    a spoon. Well-mannered patrons might use bread to push this thick sludge into
    their maw, but these kinds of patrons would probably not order this dish in the
    first place. A more common sight would be sickly pale people fishing for the
    chunks of grey meat from the bowl with their fingers, and scooping out thick
    paste alongside it. Some would even go so far as burying their ghastly face into
    the bowl, only surfacing for air once nothing is left.
